---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About HomeMaterialCalc — Free Material Calculators for US Homeowners"
  description="HomeMaterialCalc provides free material calculators for mulch, gravel, concrete, paint, flooring, tile, and more — giving US homeowners exact bag, yard, and gallon counts."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6 flex flex-wrap gap-1">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a>
      <span>›</span>
      <span class="text-gray-700">About</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">About HomeMaterialCalc</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">Free material calculators for US homeowners — mulch, gravel, concrete, paint, flooring, tile, drywall, lumber, and more.</p>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-6 text-gray-700">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is HomeMaterialCalc?</h2>
        <p>
          HomeMaterialCalc is a free collection of material calculators built for US homeowners and DIYers.
          Enter your project dimensions and get an instant, accurate quantity in the unit your supplier actually sells —
          bags, cubic yards, tons, gallons, boxes, or pallets. No guessing, no unit conversions, no wasted trips to the store.
        </p>
        <p>
          We cover <strong>12 materials</strong> across landscaping, concrete, and interior projects:
          mulch, gravel, topsoil, sand, sod, concrete, paint, flooring, tile, drywall, lumber, and pavers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Who it's for</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Homeowners</strong> planning a landscaping or remodeling project</li>
          <li><strong>DIYers</strong> who want to buy the right amount before heading to the store</li>
          <li><strong>Landscapers and contractors</strong> who need a quick estimate on the go</li>
          <li>Anyone who has Googled "how much mulch do I need" or "how many bags of concrete for a 10×10 slab"</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How the calculators work</h2>
        <p>
          Every calculator follows the same logic: measure your area, pick a depth (for bulk materials), apply the
          correct material constant, add a waste factor, and convert to the purchase unit. The math is explained
          step-by-step on each result page so you can verify it yourself.
        </p>
        <p>
          All material constants — concrete bag yields, gravel densities, paint coverage rates, mulch bag yields —
          are sourced from manufacturer specifications and industry standards. They're documented with citations on our
          <a href="/data-sources" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Data Sources</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Our commitment to accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          Calculation accuracy is the entire point of this site. We maintain a single source-of-truth constants file,
          document every formula on our <a href="/methodology" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Methodology</a> page,
          and run automated tests on every formula so a code change cannot silently break the math.
          If you find an error, <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">contact us</a> — we take it seriously.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Free to use</h2>
        <p>
          All calculators are completely free, with no signup or registration required. Results include a
          step-by-step breakdown and optional cost estimate when you enter your local price.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, corrections, or suggestions? Use our <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">contact form</a>.
          We read every message.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm">
      <a href="/data-sources"           class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Data Sources →</a>
      <a href="/how-it-works"           class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">How It Works →</a>
      <a href="/calculation-assumptions" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Calculation Assumptions →</a>
      <a href="/methodology"            class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Methodology →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
